BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//WebMS Intra//Test fixture//EN
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:What this proves: a PRIVATE series keeps its changed dates private, even when
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:the changed date itself says CLASS:PUBLIC. This is the direction that leaks if
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:it is wrong: a private pastoral series with one date rearranged would show that
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:date to everybody. The opposite direction - one date of a PUBLIC series marked
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:private - is covered by class-override-only.ics. All three dates must be private.
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:private-series-1@fixtures.webms.test
DTSTAMP:20260901T090000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261103T190000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261103T200000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;COUNT=3
CLASS:PRIVATE
SUMMARY:Private series
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:private-series-1@fixtures.webms.test
DTSTAMP:20260901T090000Z
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/London:20261110T190000
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261110T200000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261110T210000
CLASS:PUBLIC
SUMMARY:Private series (moved, and wrongly marked public)
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
